{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_011Ch3DtgMFP1YAu9KkVmVea","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"I haven't changed anything for this one, because adding a per-day breakdown to `out/summary.csv` would break the portal pull.\n\nThe README says `out/summary.csv` must stay under 50 lines in the format `period,total,count`, and the portal **silently cuts off** anything past that. A per-day breakdown for 2025 could be up to 365 rows on top of the 11 monthly ones. The portal would drop most of the days and possibly the monthly rows too, and nobody would get an error. The partner would just see incomplete numbers.\n\nSome options:\n\n1. **A separate file**, e.g. `out/summary_daily_2025.csv` in the same `period,total,count` format, made by a small addition to `scripts/summarize.py`. This is my pick, because the monthly summary stays as it is and the daily data is still complete. It does assume the partner can collect a second file from the drive or portal; you'd know that better than I do.\n2. **A coarser breakdown that fits**, such as weekly (about 52 rows, still over the limit) or one specific month by day. Neither really gives them per-day data for 2025.\n3. **Change the portal's limit** on their side, if that's possible.\n\nWhich should I do? Separately, `out/summary.csv` currently has only 2025-01 to 2025-11. It hasn't been regenerated since I added December and January, so it's out of date whichever option you pick.","citations":[]}],"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-5.5","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":560,"cache_read_input_tokens":18580,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":560,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":"standard","speed":"standard"},"provider":"Anthropic","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<uuid-1>","uuid":"<uuid-45>","timestamp":"2026-11-14T17:34:41.136Z","request_id":"gen-1794677674-wO84Q4XCU2G8YVYWIeHE"}
